Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of these Rules is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Establishment and Operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and the Enforcement Decree of that Act, and matters necessary for their enforcement.

Article 2 (Establishment of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary)
(1) One Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall be established for each coast guard station under Article 3 (1) of the Act on Establishment and Operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary (hereinafter referred to as the "Act").
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), two or more Korea Coast Guard Auxiliaries may be established for each coast guard station where the chief of the coast guard station deems it necessary in consideration of local conditions, such as population, area, and administrative districts.
(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), matters necessary for the establishment of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 3 (Name of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary)
The name of a Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 2 shall be "OOO Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary". In such cases, the name shall include the name of the jurisdiction of the coast guard station to which it belongs.

Article 4 (Commemorative Events for Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Day)
(1) As a rule, commemorative events for Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Day under Article 5 (2) of the Act shall be held on December 23 of each year: Provided, That the timing of the events may be adjusted where unavoidable circumstances prevent them from being held on that date.
(2) Commemorative events under paragraph (1) may include an awards ceremony for individuals or organizations that have made particularly significant contributions to the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary.

Article 5 (Procedures for Commissioning Members of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary, etc.)
(1) A person who wishes to be commissioned as a member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for membership in attached Form 1 to the chief of the competent coast guard station, with two photographs attached (meaning frontal upper-body photographs taken without a hat or similar headwear within six months before the application, measuring 3.5 centimeters in width and 4.5 centimeters in height).
(2) Upon receiving an application under paragraph (1), the chief of the coast guard station shall verify an extract of the resident registration record or a certificate of fact of alien registration (only where the applicant is a foreign national) through joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act: Provided, That where the applicant does not consent to verification, the chief shall require the relevant document to be attached.
(3) The chief of the coast guard station receiving an application under paragraph (1) shall decide whether to commission the applicant following deliberation by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee under Article 10, and shall notify the applicant of the result.
(4) A person notified of a decision to commission that person under paragraph (3) shall submit a consent form for the collection, use, and provision of personal information in attached Form 2 to the chief of the competent coast guard station.
(5) Upon commissioning a member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary, the chief of the coast guard station shall issue a certificate of commission in attached Form 3 and maintain a list of the members commissioned.
(6) A "person with an academic background or career experience prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries" in Article 6 (1) 4 of the Act means a person falling under any of the following:
1. A person who has obtained a master's or doctoral degree in a field related to diving, vessels, or maritime affairs;
2. A person belonging to a company, organization, or institution related to salvage, shipbuilding, maritime affairs, or fisheries;
3. A person with at least five years of service as a public official belonging to the Korea Coast Guard: Provided, That a person currently in service is excluded.
(7) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (5), details necessary for the procedures and methods for commissioning members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 6 (Grounds and Procedures for Dismissal of Members of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary, etc.)
(1) "Grounds prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries" in Article 6 (2) 6 of the Act means any of the following:
1. Where a member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary expresses an intention that it is difficult for the member to perform duties;
2. Where a member has failed, without good cause, to comply with a mobilization order under Article 10 (1) of the Act on at least three occasions during the preceding year;
3. Where a member has not participated in education and training under Article 13 (1) of the Act during the two years from the date of initial commissioning;
4. Where a member has received allowances or actual expenses under Article 14 of the Act by fraud or other improper means.
(2) Where the chief of a coast guard station determines that there are grounds for dismissal of a member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary (excluding grounds under Article 6 (2) 1 of the Act and paragraph (1) 1 of this Article), the chief shall notify the member, clearly stating the grounds.
(3) Where the chief of a coast guard station intends to dismiss a member notified of grounds for dismissal under paragraph (2), the chief shall obtain deliberation by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee under Article 10. In such cases, the member may attend the Operations Committee to state an opinion or submit a written opinion no later than the day before its meeting.
(4) Upon dismissing a member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary, the chief of a coast guard station shall notify the member (excluding a member dismissed under Article 6 (2) 1 of the Act) and the commander of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary to which the member belongs.
(5) Except as provided in paragraphs (2) through (4), details necessary for the procedures and methods for dismissal of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 7 (Organizational Structure)
(1) When organizing the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 7 (1) of the Act, the chief of a coast guard station may, according to local conditions, operate an Auxiliary dedicated to particular duties, such as vessel rescue, underwater rescue, surface rescue, aerial search, emergency medical care and administrative support, or volunteer service and publicity, or may establish an organization within an Auxiliary dedicated to particular duties.
(2) Details necessary for the organizational structure of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under paragraph (1) and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 8 (Commander and Deputy Commander)
(1) When recommending a commander and deputy commander to the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard under Article 7 (2) of the Act, the chief of a coast guard station shall obtain deliberation by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee under Article 10.
(2) A commander commissioned under Article 7 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "commander") shall exercise overall control over the affairs of the relevant Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and command and supervise its members under the command and supervision of the chief of the coast guard station.
(3) A deputy commander commissioned under Article 7 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "deputy commander") shall assist the commander and act on the commander's behalf where the commander is unable to perform duties for an unavoidable reason.

Article 9 (Terms of Office of Commander, etc.)
(1) The term of office of the commander shall be three years, and the commander may serve only one consecutive additional term.
(2) The term of office of the deputy commander shall be three years.

Article 10 (Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee)
(1) A Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Operations Committee") shall be established under the chief of a coast guard station to deliberate on important matters concerning operation of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 7 (3) of the Act.
(2) The Operations Committee shall deliberate on the following matters:
1. Commissioning and dismissal of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 6 of the Act;
2. Recommendation of the commander and deputy commander and commissioning of chiefs and squad leaders under Article 7 (2) of the Act;
3. Payment of allowances and actual expenses under Article 14 (1) of the Act;
4. Evaluation of performance records and awards for each Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and each of its members under Article 15 of the Act;
5. Payment of compensation and provision of medical treatment under Article 17 (1) and (2) of the Act;
6. Other matters necessary for operation of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary.
(3) The Operations Committee shall consist of at least five but not more than nine members, including one chairperson, with consideration given to gender. In such cases, members other than public officials under paragraph (4) 1 shall constitute a majority of all members.
(4) The head of the department responsible for Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary affairs shall serve as chairperson of the Operations Committee. The chief of the coast guard station shall appoint or commission members from among persons falling under any of the following:
1. Public officials belonging to the coast guard station;
2. Persons with at least five years of experience as members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary;
3. Persons recommended by the head of the Maritime Rescue and Salvage Association of Korea under Article 26 (1) of the Act on the Search and Rescue in Waters;
4. Members of a regional maritime search and rescue technical committee under Article 6 of the Act on the Search and Rescue in Waters;
5. Legal professionals, journalists, or persons active in civic volunteer organizations;
6. Other persons recognized by the chief of the coast guard station as having extensive knowledge and experience in maritime disaster rescue duties.
(5) The term of office of commissioned members under paragraph (4) 2 through 6 shall be two years, and they may serve only one consecutive additional term.
(6) A member of the Operations Committee shall be excluded from deliberation on an agenda item in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member or the member's spouse or former spouse is a party to the agenda item;
2. Where the member is or was a relative of a party to the agenda item.
(7) A party to an agenda item deliberated by the Operations Committee may request that a member be challenged where circumstances make it difficult to expect impartial deliberation from that member. The Operations Committee shall decide by resolution whether to accept the challenge. In such cases, the member subject to the challenge shall not participate in that resolution.
(8) Where a member falls under any ground for exclusion under paragraph (6), the member shall inform the Operations Committee of that fact and voluntarily refrain from deliberating on the relevant agenda item.
(9) The chief of a coast guard station may dismiss a member of the Operations Committee in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties due to a mental or physical disability;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct in connection with duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable due to neglect of duties, impairment of dignity, or another reason;
4. Where the member violates the duty to refrain under paragraph (8);
5. Where the member expresses an intention that it is difficult for the member to perform duties.
(10) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (9), details necessary for the composition and operation of the Operations Committee and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 11 (Duties)
"Matters prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries" in subparagraph 5 of Article 8 of the Act means the following:
1. Assistance for safety at various coastal events, such as local festivals and performances;
2. Assistance in recovery from damage to ensure residents' safety in daily life when a disaster occurs;
3. Assistance in safety management to prevent coastal accidents;
4. Other matters for which the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard deems assistance by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary necessary for the Korea Coast Guard's duties concerning aquatic rescue and relief and response to and prevention of distress accidents.

Article 12 (Uniforms)
(1) The uniforms of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 9 (1) of the Act shall be as set out in attached Table 1. The designs, specifications, and other particulars of the uniforms shall be separately determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.
(2) Article 16 of the Rules on Uniforms of Police Officials Belonging to the Korea Coast Guard shall apply mutatis mutandis to the periods for wearing the uniforms in attached Table 1.

Article 13 (Exceptions to Wearing Uniforms, etc.)
"Cases of emergency or other unavoidable reasons prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, such as rescuing a person in distress" in the proviso to Article 9 (1) of the Act means any of the following:
1. Performing duties that the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard recognizes as making it difficult to wear uniforms and carry identification cards due to the nature of the duties, such as rescuing persons in distress;
2. Being dispatched urgently to the scene of a disaster, such as a distress accident;
3. Not having received uniforms and identification cards, or having lost or damaged the uniforms and identification cards received.

Article 14 (Identification Cards, etc.)
(1) Identification cards (including electronic identification cards) under Article 9 (1) of the Act shall be as set out in attached Table 2.
(2) Upon issuing an identification card under paragraph (1), the chief of a coast guard station shall record and maintain the issuance in the register of issuance of identification cards for members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary in attached Form 4.
(3) Where a member or former member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary applies for a career certificate under Article 9 (2) of the Act, the chief of a coast guard station shall issue a certificate of career (current service) in attached Form 5 and record and maintain the issuance in the register of issuance of certificates of career (current service) in attached Form 6.

Article 15 (Matters to Be Reported by Commander)
Under the latter part of Article 10 (3) of the Act, the commander of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall report the following matters to the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, the Commissioner of a Regional Korea Coast Guard, and the chief of a coast guard station (hereinafter referred to as the "Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc."):
1. An outline of the occurrence of the accident and how the accident became known;
2. The status of human casualties and property damage;
3. The details of relevant activities and measures taken, such as aquatic rescue and relief and prevention of and response to distress accidents;
4. Other unusual matters that became known while performing duties, such as aquatic rescue and relief and prevention of and response to distress accidents.

Article 16 (Guidance on and Supervision over Service)
(1) Under Article 12 of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall guide and supervise the service of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary regarding the following matters so that they may maintain their dignity:
1. Wearing uniforms and other matters under Article 9 (1) of the Act;
2. Prohibited acts under Article 11 of the Act;
3. Education and training under Article 13 (1) of the Act;
4. Other matters determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard to maintain the dignity of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary.
(2) Where necessary for guidance and supervision under Article 12 of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. may require the relevant member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary to prepare relevant documents and submit materials.

Article 17 (Details of Management, Support, Education, and Training, etc.)
(1) Under Article 13 (1) of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall manage and support members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary regarding the following:
1. Performance records of duties under Article 8 of the Act;
2. Uniforms and identification cards under Article 9 (1) of the Act;
3. Equipment lent gratuitously under Article 14 (2) of the Act;
4. Insurance coverage for payment of compensation and medical expenses under Article 17 (3) of the Act;
5. Other matters the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard deems necessary for members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary to perform their duties.
(2) Under Article 13 (1) of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall provide members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary with at least 10 hours of education and training each year, including the following:
1. Methods of search, rescue, and salvage for each type of distress accident;
2. Safety matters concerning aquatic rescue and relief activities;
3. Support duties necessary for public-private cooperation in the event of a maritime disaster;
4. Other matters the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard deems necessary to develop the basic qualities of members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary.
(3) The Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. may develop and distribute equipment, teaching materials, and other items necessary for the education and training under paragraph (2).
(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), details necessary for the contents and methods of management, support, education, and training and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 18 (Entrustment of Management, Support, Education, and Training)
Under Article 13 (2) of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall entrust duties concerning management, support, education, and training for members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary under Article 17 (1) and (2) of these Rules to the Maritime Rescue and Salvage Association of Korea under Article 26 (1) of the Act on the Search and Rescue in Waters.

Article 19 (Payment of Allowances)
(1) Under Article 14 (1) of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall pay the following allowances to members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary who perform duties under Article 8 of the Act or participate in education and training under Article 13 (1) of the Act:
1. Dispatch allowance;
2. Education and training allowance.
(2) The standards for payment of the allowances under paragraph (1) shall be as set out in attached Table 3.
(3) A person wishing to apply for an allowance under paragraph (1) shall submit an application for dispatch allowance, etc. in attached Form 7 to the chief of the competent coast guard station, with the documents specified below attached:
1. Where payment of fuel costs is sought: Documents proving the specifications and owner of the vessel or aircraft;
2. Where any person was aboard the vessel or aircraft: Documents proving that the person was aboard the vessel or aircraft.

Article 20 (Performance-Based Awards, etc.)
(1) Under Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall evaluate the performance records of each Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and each of its members annually and maintain the results.
(2) The Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall annually select and reward Korea Coast Guard Auxiliaries and their members with outstanding evaluation results under paragraph (1), and endeavor to raise their morale.
(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), details necessary for the evaluation and management of performance records and awards for each Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and each of its members shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.

Article 21 (Application for Medical Treatment)
A member of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary who wishes to receive medical treatment under Article 3 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Establishment and Operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall submit an application for medical treatment in attached Form 8, with the documents specified below attached, to the Metropolitan City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor having jurisdiction over the place where the duties were performed or the education and training took place, after obtaining confirmation from the chief of the competent coast guard station:
1. In the case of injury (disease): A certificate of hospital treatment;
2. In the case of disability: A disability assessment certificate.

