Attached Table 3: Standards for Payment of Allowances to Members of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary (Related to Article 19 (2))
Enforcement Rules of the Act on Establishment and Operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary [Attached Table 3]

1. Dispatch allowance
(a) Activity payment: Limited to one payment per person per day, payment shall be made as follows according to activity time (measured from departure following a request for assistance to return after completion of duties) and the hourly minimum wage [meaning the higher of the hourly minimum wage under Article 5 of the Minimum Wage Act and the minimum wage for seafarers publicly notified by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries under Article 59 of the Seafarers Act (where set monthly, the amount obtained by dividing it by 240 hours and discarding the decimal part); the same shall apply hereinafter].
  1) Where activity time is eight hours or less: Basic allowance.
     Basic allowance = hourly minimum wage × eight hours. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
  2) Where activity time is eight hours or more: Basic allowance + overtime allowance.
     Overtime allowance = hourly minimum wage × excess activity time. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
(b) Fuel costs: Payment for fuel used by mobilized vessels and aircraft shall be made as follows: Provided, That no fuel costs shall be paid where fuel costs are paid by another means, such as government support.
  1) Vessels: Fuel consumption (liters) × fuel price for the relevant month. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
    (a) Fuel consumption: The smaller of the recognized fuel consumption and the fuel consumption submitted by the mobilized vessel. Recognized fuel consumption shall be calculated as follows:

| Fuel type | Calculation standard |
| --- | --- |
| Diesel | Activity time × horsepower × 0.118 liters |
| Gasoline | Activity time × horsepower × 0.209 liters |
| Heavy fuel oil, such as BA or BB oil | Activity time × horsepower × 0.106 liters |

    (b) Fuel price:
      (1) Fishing vessels: The tax-exempt fuel price supplied each month by a fisheries cooperative under the Fisheries Cooperatives Act shall apply.
      (2) Vessels other than fishing vessels: The refinery supply price of marine diesel or regular gasoline publicly disclosed by the Korea National Oil Corporation under the Korea National Oil Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea National Oil Corporation") shall apply: Provided, That for vessels using heavy fuel oil, such as BA or BB oil, the refinery supply price of marine diesel publicly disclosed by the Korea National Oil Corporation shall apply.
  2) Aircraft: Fuel consumption (liters) × fuel price for the relevant month. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
    (a) Fuel consumption: The fuel consumption recognized by the aircraft manufacturer.
    (b) Fuel price: The lower of the refinery supply price of premium gasoline publicly disclosed by the Korea National Oil Corporation and the actual transaction price.
(c) Travel expenses: Fares (transportation expenses), meal expenses, and accommodation expenses shall be paid according to the standards in item 2 of attached Table 2 of the Regulations on Travel Expenses of Public Officials.

2. Education and training allowance
(a) Mobilization payment: Education payments and training payments shall be limited to one payment per person per day and shall be paid as follows to persons who participate for at least two thirds of the total education and training time:
  1) Education payment:
    (a) In-person group education:
      (1) Where education time is at least four hours: Hourly minimum wage × eight hours. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
      (2) Where education time is less than four hours: Hourly minimum wage × four hours. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
    (b) Online education: Hourly minimum wage × education time (recognized up to eight hours). Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
  2) Training payment: Hourly minimum wage × eight hours. Any amount below 10 won shall be discarded.
(b) Fuel costs: Fuel used by vessels and aircraft mobilized for training shall be paid by applying mutatis mutandis the standards for fuel costs under the dispatch allowance in subparagraph 1 (b).
(c) Travel expenses: Fares (transportation expenses), meal expenses, and accommodation expenses incurred for education and training shall be paid according to the standards in item 2 of attached Table 2 of the Regulations on Travel Expenses of Public Officials.

