Source Supplement: Reasons for Enactment and Amendment
[Enactment]
Reasons for Enactment and Main Contents

1. Reasons for enactment
The Act on Establishment and Operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary was enacted (Act No. 19911, promulgated on January 2, 2024, effective on January 3, 2025) to prescribe matters necessary for the establishment and operation of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary and other relevant matters in order to systematically support the Korea Coast Guard's duties concerning aquatic rescue and relief and response to and prevention of distress accidents on the surface of the sea. Accordingly, these Rules prescribe matters delegated by the Act and matters necessary for its enforcement, including the scope of establishment and names of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliaries, procedures for commissioning and dismissing their members, composition and operation of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committees, and details of management, support, education, and training for members.

2. Main contents
(a) Scope of establishment and names of Korea Coast Guard Auxiliaries (draft Articles 2 and 3)
  1) One Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall be established for each coast guard station, but two or more may be established where the chief of the coast guard station deems it necessary in consideration of local conditions, such as population, area, and administrative districts.
  2) The name of a Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary shall include the name of the jurisdiction of the coast guard station to which it belongs.
(b) Procedures for commissioning and dismissing members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary, etc. (draft Articles 5 and 6)
  1) A person wishing to be commissioned shall submit an application for membership to the chief of the competent coast guard station, who shall decide whether to commission the applicant following deliberation by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee.
  2) Where grounds for dismissal of a member are deemed to exist, the chief of the coast guard station shall notify the member, clearly stating the grounds, and dismiss the member following deliberation by the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee.
(c) Organizational structure of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary (draft Article 7)
The chief of a coast guard station may, according to local conditions, operate an Auxiliary dedicated to particular duties, such as vessel rescue, underwater rescue, surface rescue, or aerial search, or establish an organization within an Auxiliary dedicated to particular duties.
(d) Composition and operation of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee (draft Article 10)
A Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary Operations Committee shall be established under the chief of a coast guard station to deliberate on important matters concerning operation of the Auxiliary, such as commissioning and dismissal of members and payment of compensation.
(e) Details of management, support, education, and training for members of the Korea Coast Guard Auxiliary (draft Article 17)
  1) The Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall provide management and support regarding such matters as performance records of Auxiliary duties, uniforms and identification cards, and equipment lent gratuitously.
  2) The Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall provide members with at least 10 hours of education and training annually, including methods of search, rescue, and salvage for each type of distress accident and safety matters concerning aquatic rescue and relief activities.
(f) Payment of allowances and payment standards (draft Article 19 and attached Table 3)
  1) The Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard, etc. shall pay a dispatch allowance or an education and training allowance to members who perform duties or participate in education and training.
  2) The dispatch allowance shall consist of an activity payment, fuel costs, and travel expenses; the education and training allowance shall consist of a mobilization payment, fuel costs, and travel expenses. The activity payment under the dispatch allowance shall be calculated using the higher of the minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Act and the minimum wage for seafarers under the Seafarers Act.
